window.docContents[141].resolve({"/References/#Type-Systems--References___-Typing-Mutable-References--Properties--Preservation___-Finally":{"contents":"We can now give the final, correct statement of the type\npreservation property:\n\ndef preservation_theorem {δ : StoreTy} {t t' : Tm} {τ : Ty} {ρ ρ' : Store} :=\n  (hTy : <{ ∅ / δ ⊢ t ⦂ τ }>) →\n  (hStoreTy : δ ⊢ ρ) →\n  (hEval : t / ρ ⟶ t' / ρ') →\n    ∃ δ', Extends δ' δ ∧ (<{ ∅ / δ' ⊢ t' ⦂ τ }>) ∧ (δ' ⊢ ρ')\n\n\n\n\nThis gives us just what we need to \"turn the\ncrank\" when applying the theorem to multi-step reduction\nsequences.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Type Systems\u0009References: Typing Mutable References\u0009Properties","header":"9.5.3. Preservation, Finally","id":"/References/#Type-Systems--References___-Typing-Mutable-References--Properties--Preservation___-Finally"}});